  "difficulty_reason": "Counted unit: the article's theorem (thm:main) (source0.tex lines 397-404, source label thm:main). The statement reads: theorem [No quintic 5+5 factorization] thm:main Let p,q Z >0 be coprime with p q and let Q p,q (t) be as in eq:Qpq . Then Q p,q (t) admits no quintic 5+5 factorization of splitting type (5,5) over / Z , i.e., there do not exist monic irreducible quintics A(t),. The retained complete proof (lines 406-425, 20 lines) is the article's own argument, retained line for line. It is a research-level argument in this field: it is not a routine verification but a complete proof whose steps (case analysis, intermediate estimates, comparison or induction arguments as the source words them) must all be carried out before the statement follows, which places it above ordinary PhD qualifying exercises, where such results are quoted rather than proved.",
